1. Final folder structure
FullStackPractice/
│
├── frontend/
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── App.jsx
│   │   ├── main.jsx
│   │   └── index.css
│   ├── vite.config.js
│   └── package.json
│
└── backend/
    ├── server.js
    ├── package.json
    └── .env


Your existing frontend setup stays unchanged. We'll connect it to this backend.
2. Backend package.json
Create a folder called backend, then create package.json inside it.

{
  "name": "fullstack-practice-backend",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Minimal Express and MongoDB CRUD backend",
  "main": "server.js",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.js",
    "dev": "nodemon server.js"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "cors": "^2.8.5",
    "dotenv": "^16.4.7",
    "express": "^4.21.2",
    "mongoose": "^8.9.5"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "nodemon": "^3.1.9"
  }
}



Install the dependencies by opening a terminal inside backend:
npm install

5. Start your backend
In the VS Code terminal:
cd backend
npm install
npm start

3. Backend .env
Create a file named .env inside backend.
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://YOUR_USERNAME:YOUR_PASSWORD@YOUR_CLUSTER.mongodb.net/fullstack_practice


